<h3>3. Necessary Documents </h3><p><span style="color: #ff0000;">Please complete Step 1 and Step 2 by the deadline.<br>* Late, ineligible or incomplete applications will NOT be accepted for any reason.</span><br><span style="color: #ff0000;">* Some applications have incomplete application documents or missing information. Incomplete applications can cause delays in the overall schedule, so please be sure to review <a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/common/is/ryugakusei/www/common_mistakes_e.pdf" target="_blank" style="color: #ff0000;">the list of common mistakes</a>, the notes on the ISEPTUFS Application Checklist, and the samples for each document before submitting. Both the applicant and the coordinator are required to review the application documents.</span></p><p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Step 1 Application for the exchange program (ISEPTUFS)</span></p><ul class="wm-ul-circle">
<li>Applicants’ Application: <a href="https://business.form-mailer.jp/fms/a448b271348648" target="_blank">Form mailer</a></li>
<li><span style="color: #ff0000;"><span style="color: #000000;">Documents need to be submitted by the coordinator at home university via designated online form.<br>Coordinator’s online submission: <a href="https://business.form-mailer.jp/fms/062215f7348744" target="_blank">Form mailer</a><br></span></span></li>
<li><span style="color: #ff0000;"><span style="color: #000000;">Combine the following documents into one PDF file per one applicant when submitting online .</span><br><span style="color: #000000;">All the documents should be written in English or Japanese.</span><br><span style="color: #000000;">Please use the latest format by downloading from the below.</span><br></span></li>
</ul><ol class="wm-ol-def">
<li><a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/common/is/ryugakusei/www/applicationchecklist.pdf" target="_blank">ISEPTUFS Application Checklist</a> (<a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/common/is/ryugakusei/www/applicationchecklist_sample.pdf" target="_blank">sample</a>)</li>
<li><a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/common/is/ryugakusei/www/Participation_agreement.pdf" target="_blank">Participation Agreement</a> (<a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/common/is/ryugakusei/www/Participation_agreement_sample.pdf" target="_blank">sample</a>)</li>
<li><a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/common/is/ryugakusei/www/Certificate_of_Health.pdf" target="_blank">Certificate of Health</a> (<a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/common/is/ryugakusei/www/Certificate_of_Health_Sample.pdf" target="_blank">sample</a>)</li>
<li>Latest official academic record at home university written in English or Japanese (<a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/common/is/ryugakusei/www/ISEPTUFS_Academic_Record_Sample.pdf" target="_blank">sample</a>)<br><span style="text-decoration: underline;">*Submit the latest transcript issued by home university after the application starts<br></span> which includes following:<br>- All credits and grades for at least one academic term<br>- Date of issue (if not specified, attach a letter by home university indicating it was issued after the application acceptance period began)<br>*All applicants: <span style="text-decoration: underline;">Highlight the most recent semester’s grades on the submitted transcript in YELLOW</span> for ISEPTUFS GPA.<br>*JASSO applicants only: <span style="text-decoration: underline;">Underline the previous academic year's grades in RED</span> for JASSO GPA. If the previous academic year's grades are not available, underline the most recent semester’s grades in red. (If it is not underlined in red, it is assumed that the applicants do not wish to apply for the JASSO Scholarship regardless of answer in the online application form.)</li>
<li>Document proving English /Japanese language proficiency (Certificate of the specified test/ Recommendation letter from home university)<br>Type of acceptable certificate: <br>◎English: TOEFL iBT, IELTS, TOEIC L&amp;R and S&amp;W, Cambridge English<br>　*Reference: <a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/common/is/ryugakusei/www/CEFRComparisonChart.pdf" target="_blank">Comparison of qualifications and examinations with the CEFR</a><br>◎Japanese: Japanese Language Proficiency Test N2 or above<br>Those who cannot submit the certificates above need to submit a recommendation letter about the language proficiency issued by the home university.<br>　*<a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/common/is/ryugakusei/www/ISEPTUFS_Language_Recommendation_Letter_Sample.pdf" target="_blank">sample of recommendation letter</a> (<a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/common/is/ryugakusei/www/ISEPTUFS_Language_Recommendation_Letter_Format.doc" target="_blank">format</a>)<br>　*<a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/common/is/ryugakusei/www/ISEPTUFS_Language_Recommendation_Letter_Native_Sample.pdf" target="_blank">sample of recommendation letter *For native speaker of English/Japanese and students whose degree program is taught entirely in English or Japanese</a> (<a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/common/is/ryugakusei/www/ISEPTUFS_Language_Recommendation_Letter_Native_Format.doc" target="_blank">format</a>)</li>
<li><a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/common/is/ryugakusei/www/ISEPTUFS_study_plan.doc" target="_blank">Study Plan</a></li>
<li>A copy of Passport</li>
</ol><p>●Please double-check the application documents carefully before submitting them. Please refer to <a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/common/is/ryugakusei/www/common_mistakes_e.pdf" target="_blank">the list of common mistakes</a> as well.</p><p><em><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Step 2 Application for Certificate of Eligibility</span></em></p><p>Certificate of Eligibility (CoE) is an essential document for visa application. Applicants are requested to enter your required information through the CoE Web Application System and submit required documents. Please enter the information by an applicant so that there is no wrong information.</p><ul class="wm-ul-circle">
<li>Web Application: <a href="https://v4.coe-service.cloud/application/login/organization" target="_blank">CoE Web Application System</a>*Please refer to the manuals sent by TUFS.</li>
</ul><h3>4. Language requirements</h3><p>Since students take classes conducted in English or Japanese, they need to have the appropriate English or Japanese ability. </p><p>English: CEFR (Common European Framework of Reference for Languages) B2</p><p>or</p><p>Japanese: N2 of Japanese Language Proficiency Test (JLPT)</p><p>Reference: <a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/common/is/ryugakusei/www/CEFRComparisonChart.pdf" target="_blank">Comparison of qualifications and examinations with the CEFR</a> </p><h3>5. GPA requirement</h3><p>2.0/4.0 or higher</p><p>*GPA should be calculated using the grades of the previous semester at the time of application.For the details, refer to the fact sheet.</p><p>Coordinators who have any questions about conversion to a 4.0 scale GPA, please contact TUFS Student Exchange Division (it is preferable to contact us before applying). TUFS will not respond to GPA inquiries from applicants.</p><h3>6. About scholarships</h3><p>The Ministry of Education of Japan supports the Japan Students Service Organization (JASSO) Scholarship, which international exchange students coming to TUFS receive each year. Basic information regarding the scholarship program is provided below. Please note that the chances of being chosen as the recipient of JASSO scholarship are very low.</p><p>Student Eligibility</p><ol class="wm-ol-def">
<li>Students from all countries that have diplomatic relations with Japan.（Students from Taiwan and Palestine are acceptable. Students with Japanese nationality (including dual nationality) are not eligible.）</li>
<li>Students accepted by Japanese school under a student exchange agreement or other student exchange arrangement with their home school.</li>
<li>Students not having the financial means to study in Japan.</li>
<li>Students eligible for "Student Visa". （For study in Japan for 90 days or less, Japanese school will arrange the status of residence.）</li>
<li>Students, upon termination of the period of study in Japan, will complete their studies at their home school.</li>
<li>Students demonstrating excellent academic and personal records at their home school.</li>
<li>Students receiving more than 80,000 JPY per month in total from other scholarships for study in Japan are ineligible for this scholarship.</li>
</ol><p>When students are selected as a scholarship recipient, they must submit all required documents to TUFS during their exchange program and when they finish their program at TUFS.<br>Students must send their transcript to TUFS when they transfer the credits obtained at TUFS to their home university after they finish the exchange program. If there are incomplete or missing procedures or documents, students may be required to return the money to JASSO.</p><h3>7. Dormitory</h3><p>Presently we have three dormitories on campus of the university. However, the possibility exists that students cannot receive accommodation at these dormitories because of an increasing number of international students. Those who cannot be accommodated on campus will need to find and live in alternative apartments off campus. The average rent off campus per month is around 50,000~80,000 JPY. Please understand this fact beforehand.</p><p>For more information about on-campus dormitory, please refer to the following:<br><a href="/english/student/international_student/housing.html">https://www.tufs.ac.jp/english/student/international_student/housing.html</a><br>Note: Check-in is only available on the designated dates and times.<br>- For spring entry: two days in early April<br>- For fall entry: two days at the end of September<br>Those who live in the dormitory must arrive in Japan by the check-in dates. The check-in schedule will be announced at the time of acceptance (for spring entry: December in the previous year, for fall all entry: June).</p><h3>8. <a href="https://www.tufs.ac.jp/english/admission/non-degree/exchange/faq.html">Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</a></h3><h3>9. Contact Information</h3><p>Student Exchange Division<br>Tokyo University of Foreign Studies<br>3-11-1 Asahi-cho, Fuchu-shi, Tokyo 183-8534, JAPAN<br>Email: inbound[at]tufs.ac.jp (Please change [at] to @.)<br><br></p>





